<p>In general, your core element's anomalies should make sense when considered altogether. Unconnected anomalous qualities can feel disconnected and confusing for a reader; a platypus that speaks French and poops iPhones is going to be considerably more difficult to fit in a story than, say, a surfer who can talk to dolphins.</p>
<p>How would that arc be represented in the rest of the article? A final interview can certainly help cement emotional growth, but we need to see how that growth began in the first place. <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/cybersqyd" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5336470); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5336470&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606638653" alt="cybersqyd" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5336470)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/cybersqyd" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5336470); return false;">cybersqyd</a></span> puts it much better than I could below.</p>

