<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[+]&nbsp;Open&nbsp;for&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>A number of incident logs in which he realizes that the world around him has changed, and warps reality to change it back.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>So like, what do these actually look like? My concern is that you're in a situation where they don't add a lot individually but they're also not really hugely interesting; and so you both want short logs to not dwell on them much but also longer logs to really try and show why they are interesting; and neither option quite works.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>culminating in an interview in which he is finally informed of his abilities, and chooses to assist the foundation in making sure he is unaware of when he shifts, especially after reflecting on the harm he's caused.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>so like, this is fine but like&#8230;if he realises he's caused a lot of harm, and there's implication he's in full control of his reality bending abilities, why does he need to be kept unaware of when shifts occur? Surely he can just like&#8230;understand that is what is going on and not get mad?</p>
<p>More to the point, why does he even alter reality? Like I get him wanting to shift stuff back towards what it should be on paper but it doesn't seem like there's any changes that actually materially affect him since he's in foundation containment in all the cases and there's not like a big driving force like &quot;my wife died in 6/7 of the realities and i want her to be around still&quot;?</p>
<p>I think my big concern is that the narrative arc feels excessively shallow and very late: the actual growth of the SCP doesn't kick in until the final act when he's told about the reality bending powers and then it immediately all happens then; and it feels like the earlier incident logs just&#8230;are filler material to bridge the gap instead of like, actually adding to what you want to do here?</p>
</div>
