<p>I think the big thing that I didn't portray well enough in the original post, and will try to correct, is that the activation of the powers is almost completely unconscious and automatic. If he notices a change, he simply causes the change to no longer be there. The only way to stop it is for him to not notice changes, hence the constant monitoring and goal of keeping the various containments synced.</p>
<p>I agree that the narrative is a bit shallow and late. The new focus is much more on the foundation attempting to gaslight him so even if he does notice the changes, he thinks they're more in his own head, rather than reality being different. I also think the logs will be shorter and much more focused than I first intended. I've reworked the post to show the current idea for the chain of events, which should be a lot more definite and specific.</p>

