<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>This still feels like it's lacking something and I think it's a just a like&#8230;sense of escalation? Like a feeling of it building up to something and having a big scene where everything pays off? Like there's kinda a progression through the logs with the events getting more severe and the foundation eventually changing track to try a different approach; but it feels&#8230;unguided? Like it's a sequence of things that happen over a story being driven there by a purpose; part of which I think is because of the focus on the SCP and it's actions being involuntary.</p>
<p>I think what this really needs is like&#8230;a central character or group of characters who like are in charge of handling the outcome of each of the incidents and with like, trying stuff to reduce their severity; perhaps with the overall angle being something like &quot;their initial attempts failed because they didn't work with the SCP and it was only together they succeeded&quot; kinda thing but?</p>
<p>It's very possible the issue is just the idea doesn't vibe with me though so like, you may want to ask a few other experienced reviewers.</p>
